WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:06.244
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online English for Academic Purposes.

2
00:00:06.544 --> 00:00:10.105
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:10.405 --> 00:00:16.784
Unit two: Academic Vocabulary. Today you will learn and use common academic words correctly.

4
00:00:17.084 --> 00:00:19.759
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:24.026
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.883 --> 00:00:25.884
Analyse.

7
00:00:26.883 --> 00:00:29.579
Analyse means to study something in detail.

8
00:00:30.183 --> 00:00:31.718
Analyse the results.

9
00:00:32.317 --> 00:00:35.073
Your turn. Say: Analyse.

10
00:00:37.933 --> 00:00:38.992
Analyse.

11
00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:40.705
Evidence.

12
00:00:41.717 --> 00:00:44.355
Evidence means facts that support an idea.

13
00:00:44.950 --> 00:00:46.590
Give evidence for your claim.

14
00:00:47.183 --> 00:00:49.511
Your turn. Say: Evidence.

15
00:00:52.367 --> 00:00:53.356
Evidence.

16
00:00:54.117 --> 00:00:55.234
Significant.

17
00:00:56.250 --> 00:00:59.248
Significant means important or large enough to matter.

18
00:00:59.850 --> 00:01:01.791
There is a significant change.

19
00:01:02.383 --> 00:01:04.978
Your turn. Say: Significant.

20
00:01:07.833 --> 00:01:08.962
Significant.

21
00:01:09.717 --> 00:01:10.660
Approach.

22
00:01:11.650 --> 00:01:13.928
Approach means a way of doing something.

23
00:01:14.517 --> 00:01:16.005
Try a new approach.

24
00:01:16.617 --> 00:01:18.909
Your turn. Say: Approach.

25
00:01:21.767 --> 00:01:22.733
Approach.

26
00:01:23.483 --> 00:01:24.403
Factor.

27
00:01:25.417 --> 00:01:27.892
Factor means one thing that affects a result.

28
00:01:28.483 --> 00:01:30.088
Cost is one factor.

29
00:01:30.683 --> 00:01:32.906
Your turn. Say: Factor.

30
00:01:35.767 --> 00:01:36.652
Factor.

31
00:01:37.417 --> 00:01:38.220
Issue.

32
00:01:39.217 --> 00:01:41.890
Issue means an important topic or problem.

33
00:01:42.483 --> 00:01:44.320
Pollution is a global issue.

34
00:01:44.917 --> 00:01:47.360
Your turn. Say: Issue.

35
00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:50.969
Issue.

36
00:01:51.717 --> 00:01:52.695
Indicate.

37
00:01:53.683 --> 00:01:55.845
Indicate means to show or suggest.

38
00:01:56.450 --> 00:01:58.403
The data indicate a rise.

39
00:01:59.017 --> 00:02:01.634
Your turn. Say: Indicate.

40
00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:05.524
Indicate.

41
00:02:06.283 --> 00:02:07.331
Consequence.

42
00:02:08.317 --> 00:02:10.699
Consequence means a result of an action.

43
00:02:11.283 --> 00:02:13.178
A bad consequence followed.

44
00:02:13.783 --> 00:02:16.436
Your turn. Say: Consequence.

45
00:02:19.300 --> 00:02:20.429
Consequence.

46
00:02:21.233 --> 00:02:24.826
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:25.683 --> 00:02:28.716
Visal, why is academic vocabulary important?

48
00:02:29.817 --> 00:02:36.335
The same academic words appear in many subjects. If you know them, you read faster and write more clearly.

49
00:02:37.450 --> 00:02:38.625
How do I learn them?

50
00:02:39.717 --> 00:02:51.587
Learn each word with its family, such as analyse, analysis and analyst. Notice the words that go with it, such as significant difference or strong evidence.

51
00:02:52.683 --> 00:02:54.230
Can I use them in speech?

52
00:02:55.317 --> 00:03:04.053
Yes, but use them naturally. Choose a precise word instead of a vague one, for example factor instead of thing.

53
00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:06.793
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:07.650 --> 00:03:11.054
Grammar focus: Word families and collocations.

55
00:03:11.354 --> 00:03:12.576
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:13.283 --> 00:03:15.933
The analysis shows a significant change.

57
00:03:16.817 --> 00:03:19.025
Researchers analyse the evidence.

58
00:03:19.967 --> 00:03:27.971
Learn word families: analyse is a verb, analysis is a noun and analytical is an adjective. Learn common word partners too.

59
00:03:28.717 --> 00:03:32.658
Be careful! Don't say: The analysis are very clear.

60
00:03:34.600 --> 00:03:37.343
Say: The analysis is very clear.

61
00:03:37.643 --> 00:03:39.375
Analysis is singular.

62
00:03:40.167 --> 00:03:43.376
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:44.167 --> 00:03:45.899
A Vocabulary Notebook.

64
00:03:46.199 --> 00:03:49.116
Sreyna keeps a notebook of academic words.

65
00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:53.237
For each word she writes the noun, verb and adjective.

66
00:03:54.233 --> 00:03:57.487
She also notes common partners such as strong evidence.

67
00:03:58.500 --> 00:04:01.788
Every weekend she uses five words in a short paragraph.

68
00:04:02.800 --> 00:04:05.229
After a month her reading is much faster.

69
00:04:06.333 --> 00:04:10.161
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:11.017 --> 00:04:12.958
The noun of analyse is blank.

71
00:04:13.258 --> 00:04:17.666
A, analyses it. B, analytic. C, analysis.

72
00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:23.176
The answer is C: analysis.

73
00:04:24.317 --> 00:04:26.409
Strong blank supports a claim.

74
00:04:26.709 --> 00:04:30.072
A, evidence. B, weather. C, colour.

75
00:04:33.633 --> 00:04:35.935
The answer is A: evidence.

76
00:04:37.083 --> 00:04:38.816
A factor affects a blank.

77
00:04:39.116 --> 00:04:42.166
A, window. B, result. C, shoe.

78
00:04:45.700 --> 00:04:47.781
The answer is B: result.

79
00:04:48.917 --> 00:04:50.498
Indicate means to blank.

80
00:04:50.798 --> 00:04:54.092
A, hide. B, break. C, show.

81
00:04:57.633 --> 00:04:59.343
The answer is C: show.

82
00:05:00.483 --> 00:05:02.518
Sreyna writes new words in a blank.

83
00:05:02.818 --> 00:05:05.949
A, notebook. B, kitchen. C, garden.

84
00:05:09.500 --> 00:05:11.244
The answer is A: notebook.

85
00:05:12.433 --> 00:05:15.608
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:16.450 --> 00:05:18.403
How do you learn academic words?

87
00:05:27.217 --> 00:05:28.682
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:28.982 --> 00:05:40.612
I learn each word with its family and common partners. I write the noun, verb and adjective in a notebook. Then I use new words in a short paragraph every week.

89
00:05:40.912 --> 00:05:42.644
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:43.550 --> 00:05:48.385
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and word families and collocations.

91
00:05:48.685 --> 00:05:53.114
Today's value is diligence. Check the details carefully before you commit.

92
00:05:53.414 --> 00:05:55.903
See you in Unit three. Goodbye!

93
00:05:56.203 --> 00:06:00.086
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

